{"name":"Lantana Lime","hex":"#d7eccd","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lantana","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any member of the genus Lantana of perennial verbenas with aromatic flower clusters."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lantana"},{"term":"lime","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any inorganic material containing calcium, usually calcium oxide (quicklime) or calcium hydroxide (slaked lime).","Any gluey or adhesive substance that traps or captures; sometimes a synonym for birdlime."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To treat with calcium hydroxide or calcium oxide (lime).","To smear with birdlime.\n To ensnare, catch, entrap."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lime"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lantana","blocks":[{"text":"Lantana is a genus of about 150 species of perennial flowering plants in the verbena family, Verbenaceae. They are native to tropical regions of the Americas but exist as an introduced species in numerous areas, especially in the Australian-Pacific region, South and Northeastern part of India. The genus includes both herbaceous plants and shrubs growing to 0.5–2 m (1.6–6.6 ft) tall. Their common names are shrub verbenas or lantanas. The generic name originated in Late Latin, where it refers to the unrelated Viburnum lantana."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/LantanaFlowerLeaves.jpg/330px-LantanaFlowerLeaves.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lantana","wikidata":"Q1096635"},{"title":"Lime (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Lime is a color that is a shade of yellow-green, so named because it is a representation of the color of the citrus fruit lime. It is the color that is in between the web color chartreuse and yellow on the color wheel. Alternate names for this color included yellow-green, lemon-lime, lime green, or bitter lime."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/AosaHGkyuai_%28cropped%29_3.jpg/330px-AosaHGkyuai_%28cropped%29_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lime_(color)","wikidata":"Q906936"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Lantana-Violet.jpg/500px-Lantana-Violet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Lantana-Violet.jpg/1280px-Lantana-Violet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Lantana-Violet.jpg/500px-Lantana-Violet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Lantana Violet color from Arecode, Kerala, India","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALantana-Violet.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Yellow_Lantana_Flower.jpg/500px-Yellow_Lantana_Flower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Yellow_Lantana_Flower.jpg/1280px-Yellow_Lantana_Flower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Yellow_Lantana_Flower.jpg/500px-Yellow_Lantana_Flower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Yellow color Lantana flower from Neeleswaram, Kozhikode, Kerala, India","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AYellow_Lantana_Flower.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Lantana_Invasion_of_abandoned_citrus_plantation_Sdey_Hemed_Israel.JPG/500px-Lantana_Invasion_of_abandoned_citrus_plantation_Sdey_Hemed_Israel.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16